1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,792
What if every lie left a visible thread?

2
00:00:02,832 --> 00:00:05,309
A kid says, I didn't touch the cookies,

3
00:00:05,349 --> 00:00:07,825
and a bright red thread shoots from his

4
00:00:07,865 --> 00:00:09,955
mouth straight to the cookie jar.

5
00:00:09,995 --> 00:00:10,407
Busted.

6
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:15,794
Suddenly, a first date turns into a spider web.

7
00:00:15,834 --> 00:00:17,401
I love hiking, he says,

8
00:00:17,441 --> 00:00:19,567
and a thread loops to his sofa.

9
00:00:19,607 --> 00:00:21,594
She claims she's not nervous,

10
00:00:21,634 --> 00:00:24,179
and a thread ties to her shaking cup.

11
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:27,831
At the office it gets worse.

12
00:00:27,871 --> 00:00:30,437
Great idea, boss, says every employee,

13
00:00:30,477 --> 00:00:33,181
and fifty red threads pile up around the

14
00:00:33,221 --> 00:00:36,954
meeting table like a very cranky cat's yarn collection.

15
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:39,152
Politicians struggle most.

16
00:00:39,192 --> 00:00:41,362
Their threads shoot into the sky,

17
00:00:41,402 --> 00:00:42,903
tangle with each other,

18
00:00:42,943 --> 00:00:45,985
and form a giant red knot above the town hall.

19
00:00:46,025 --> 00:00:48,865
People begin to bring scissors to speeches.

20
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:52,281
Honestly, a world with visible lies might sound

21
00:00:52,321 --> 00:00:53,356
like a nightmare.

22
00:00:53,396 --> 00:00:55,062
In this thought experiment,

23
00:00:55,102 --> 00:00:58,286
it just forces everyone to try something different:

24
00:00:58,326 --> 00:00:59,677
tell the truth gently.

25
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:01,289
Here is the twist.

26
00:01:01,329 --> 00:01:03,253
White lies leave pink threads,

27
00:01:03,293 --> 00:01:04,105
thin as hair.

28
00:01:04,145 --> 00:01:06,724
Your sweater's lovely, says your cousin,

29
00:01:06,764 --> 00:01:09,344
and the pink thread curls like a ribbon.

30
00:01:09,384 --> 00:01:12,356
Everyone starts wearing their ribbons proudly.

31
00:01:12,850 --> 00:01:13,527
Years pass.

32
00:01:13,567 --> 00:01:16,132
People learn that honesty isn't cruelty,

33
00:01:16,172 --> 00:01:17,761
and kindness isn't lying.

34
00:01:17,801 --> 00:01:20,106
The sky fills with threads at first,

35
00:01:20,146 --> 00:01:23,233
then slowly fewer, until one quiet morning there

36
00:01:23,273 --> 00:01:24,275
are almost none.

37
00:01:24,750 --> 00:01:26,232
At last, a child says,

38
00:01:26,272 --> 00:01:29,070
I love you, and no thread appears at all.

39
00:01:29,110 --> 00:01:30,385
Just a little glow.

40
00:01:30,425 --> 00:01:31,976
The whole street stops,

41
00:01:32,016 --> 00:01:33,568
looks up, and for once,

42
00:01:33,608 --> 00:01:36,059
the sky is perfectly clear and true.
